# Viewport-safe popovers and dropdowns

Never position floating menus with raw `top: rect.bottom + 4` or `absolute top-full` alone when the menu can extend past the viewport.

## Required approach

1. Use `getFixedDropdownStyle()` from `@/lib/dropdown-utils` for any `fixed` menu positioning.
2. Use `useFixedDropdownPosition()` or `FixedDropdownMenu` / `FixedSelectDropdown` so menus re-position on scroll and resize.
3. Portal menus to `document.body` when they must escape overflow containers.

## Avoid

- Inline `style={{ top: rect.bottom + 4, left: rect.left }}` without flip/clamp logic
- `absolute top-full` for menus that may open near the bottom or right edge of the screen
- Computing position once at render without scroll/resize listeners

## Pick a component

- Select lists: `FixedSelectDropdown`
- Searchable entity pickers: `SearchableEntityDropdown`
- Time/date pickers: `FixedTimePickerDropdown`, `FixedDatePickerDropdown`
- Custom menu content: `FixedDropdownMenu`
- Display column toggles: `DisplayPopoverPanel`

Pass realistic `estimatedHeight` and `minWidth`. Use `align="right"` when the trigger is right-aligned.
